      <activity id="e0ec504f-4051-57de-b0a5-0f423805a6e9" activityNameId="855e0c66-f72d-5af9-803a-faac24a6e7e2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Sawn timber, softwood, raw, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Sawn timber, softwood, raw, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant
The volume refers to the wood not including the bark. The multi-output process "sawing / debarking, softwood, at plant delivers the three coproducts "sawn timber, softwood, raw, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant", "industrial residue wood, softwood, plant-debarked, u=70%, at plant" and "bark chips, softwood, u=140%, at plant". Allocation is based on the over-all proceeds of the process.;
UUID: 33819127-75eb-3787-ab01-a93944b07317
Includes transports from forest, sawing, and debarking at sawmill.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Technology mix used in Germany 1986
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumption that Germany is representative for central Europe is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_33819127-75eb-3787-ab01-a93944b07317.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
